---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;

const applications = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Scholarliness',
    copy: 'Use abundant machine cognition as examiner, critic and practice partner to strengthen source judgment, conceptual precision, calibration, synthesis and defensible authority.',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Software engineering',
    copy: 'Attach learning to live engineering work: architecture, debugging, testing, performance, security and systems understanding should grow alongside AI-assisted delivery.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Engineering leadership',
    copy: 'Use simulation, pre-commitment, adversarial review and real outcomes to improve technical strategy, delegation, coaching, stakeholder alignment and judgment under uncertainty.',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'Nemosyne',
    copy: 'Use AI aggressively for discovery first, then reconstruct and selectively rebuild surviving ideas until the durable system becomes understandable, testable and responsibly ownable.',
  },
];
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">An open practice of capability expansion</p>
      <h1>Use abundance to attack real constraints, beginning with your own.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agalmic Research is becoming a personal capability laboratory before it is a claim about the world. The practice is simple: identify what is actually limiting useful action, inherit the best existing knowledge and tools, use available abundance against that constraint, and test whether durable capability increased.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={internal('practice')}>See the current practice</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={internal('results')}>What has survived inquiry?</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current orientation</p>
      <blockquote>Seek contribution before novelty. Seek novelty only where contribution requires discovery.</blockquote>
      <p>Research remains valuable as disciplined inquiry: lineage, testing, criticism, provenance, correction and handoff. It does not have to be the primary product. A useful tool, stronger human capability, a reusable implementation, a better route through existing knowledge or a well-supported negative result can all be worthwhile outcomes.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Inward first</p>
        <h2>Turn the practitioner into the first testbed.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The immediate question is not whether Agalmic Research constitutes a new academic field. It is whether its operating principles improve real capability in real work.</p>
        <p>When AI makes one activity cheap, the response should not automatically be to produce more of it. The useful question is which complementary constraint now matters most: understanding, judgment, subject mastery, implementation, leadership, verification, attention, coordination or something else.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Apply abundant capability against the current binding constraint, not merely against whatever it can most easily accelerate.</strong></p></div>
        <p><a href={internal('practice')}>Open the Personal Capability Practice →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Inheritance</p>
        <h2>Start from what humanity already knows.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Finding prior art is a gain in available capability, not a loss of intellectual territory.</p>
        <p>The programme increasingly treats existing theory, open-source software, standards, curricula, datasets and documented practice as inherited infrastructure. Where someone else has already paid part of the discovery cost, the default move is to understand, reuse and contribute back rather than rename or rebuild unnecessarily.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>We do not need to own an idea to advance it.</strong></p></div>
        <p><a href={internal('lineage')}>Explore the intellectual lineage →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Correction record</p>
        <h2>Make it obvious when the project changes its mind.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">A research programme should accumulate constraints, not only vocabulary.</p>
        <p>The public results record now separates object-level findings and corrections from the machinery used to produce them. Generic epistemic handoff has been narrowed by prior art; the economics of epistemic abundance has not yet survived as a distinct economic primitive; and Nemosyne has an explicit boundary around the claims it can actually test.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>If lineage, formalization or experiment kills one of our concepts, that is a successful use of the method.</strong></p></div>
        <p><a href={internal('results')}>Open Results & Retired Claims →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Current applications</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Attach the practice to needs that already matter.</h2>
          <p>The current domains are deliberately practical. Capability formation should happen inside real work wherever possible.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        {applications.map((item) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="card-kicker">{item.n}</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.copy}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Nemosyne</p>
        <h2>Discovery first. Epistemic reconstruction second.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Nemosyne does not need to become a coding curriculum while its conceptual search space is still moving.</p>
        <p>In the discovery phase, AI can generate prototypes, explore architectures and expose adjacent possibilities faster than a human could responsibly learn every implementation detail. Those outputs should remain explicitly provisional, with assumptions, provenance and roads not taken preserved.</p>
        <p>When a direction survives, the mode changes. Critical internals can then be derived, interrogated, refactored or rebuilt until the human curator can explain the architecture, inspect the evidence, understand the failure modes and defend the durable decisions.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Prototype to discover. Reconstruct to understand. Operate only what can be responsibly defended or appropriately handed off.</strong></p></div>
        <p><a href="https://nemosyne.world">Visit nemosyne.world ↗</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Research still matters</p>
        <h2>Keep the discipline. Drop the need to claim territory.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Claims still need lineage, explicit assumptions, evidence or argument, criticism and honest epistemic status. Provenance still matters. External expertise still matters. Negative results still matter.</p>
        <p class="large">The change is in what those practices serve.</p>
        <p>They serve better understanding, safer reuse, stronger capability and useful contribution. Papers are one possible output among software, protocols, curricula, datasets, demonstrations, corrections, handoffs and personal learning.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('explore')}>Explore the accumulated research record →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Contribution outward</p>
        <h2>Let useful things escape.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>When inward practice creates something genuinely reusable, the programme can publish it, release it, document it or contribute it upstream. Outward contribution is an exit path from successful work, not a requirement that every exploration become a public claim.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>A defensible increase in available capability matters more than a claim of originality.</strong></p></div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('publications')}>Public outputs</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={internal('frontier')}>Current frontier</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
